<title>POLAND: Polish m/m industrial output down 2.8 pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>Polish m/m industrial output down 2.8 pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's industrial output (undajusted) fell 2.8 percent in February after a 3.2 percent fall in January, but was 8.7 percent higher than in February 1996, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>Industrial output in the January-February period was 9.5 percent higher than in the same period last year.  </p>
<p> POLISH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT	    FEB 97     JAN 97     FEB 96</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	     -2.8	 -3.2(3.4)   -2.7</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)			8.7	  8.9(8.6)    8.7</p>
<p> index (mthly avge 1994=100)	  20.5	 23.4	  10.3</p>
<p> mining m/m change		     -10.2	  8.3(7.5)   -8.2</p>
<p> mining yr/yr change		    -2.2	  0.0(-0.8)   4.7</p>
<p> manufacturing m/m change	     -1.5	 -4.7(-4.8)  -2.1</p>
<p> manufacturing yr/yr change	   11.4	 10.9(10.7)  10.3</p>
<p> utilities m/m change		   -5.8	 -0.8(-0.7)  -2.3</p>
<p> utilities yr/yr change		 -1.0	  2.7(2.8)    2.2</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>NOTES - Revised data in brackets. February 1997 had 21 working days, February 1996 22 working days and January 1997 had 23 working days.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
